      "body": "Hey @denmalley, really sorry for the trouble here \u2014 thanks a lot for the detailed report, it helped us track this down. \ud83d\ude4f\n\n**Root cause:** We found that the weather widget displays \"No integration data available\" whenever the `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION` environment variable is enabled in your compose file. The weather widget correctly stops making outbound calls when the flag is on, but the city search behind the dropdown was not hooked up to the same flag \u2014 so you could pick any city and the widget would still show no data.\n\nThe fix (PR #6674) makes the location search respect that flag too, and shows a clear explanation on the widget when external connections are disabled. It should address exactly what you're seeing.\n\nCould you please give it a try with the preview image from the PR?\n\n```bash\ndocker pull ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr-test:pr-6674\n```\n\nRun that image on your setup (same config/volumes). It should no longer show \"No integration data available\" \u2014 either the widget will show data, or you'll get a clear message that external connections are disabled.\n\nIf you're not setting `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION` to `true` at all, then the cause is likely that your setup cannot reach `api.open-meteo.com` at all (e.g. blocked by a firewall). Let us know what you find after trying. Thanks again!",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
